    "result_text": "The build succeeds and the test passes. Let me verify the full test count reflects everything ran (only one test class exists in the project, which is expected).\n\nThe implementation is complete and green. Here's a summary of the change:\n\n## What the spec required\nWhen a create-owner request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the app should (1) allow an owner at an address already used by a same-last-name owner (this part already existed) and (2) assign that owner **and** the existing same-household owner a shared, stable `householdId`, returning it on the owner.\n\n## Changes made\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `householdId` read-only output field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it back to clients.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `household_id` column with getter/setter.\n\n**DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table so the field persists on every profile (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n**`service/HouseholdIdGenerator.java`** (new) \u2014 A small component with a single responsibility: derive the *stable, shared* identifier deterministically from the normalized last name + address (SHA-256 \u2192 16 upper-case hex chars). Reuses the existing `HouseholdNormalizer` so the household-identity comparison stays consistent across the codebase.\n\n**`service/ClinicService[Impl].java`** \u2014 Added `joinHousehold(Owner)`: finds the existing same-household members, reuses an existing `householdId` if one is present (otherwise generates one), back-fills any members that lack it, sets it on the joining owner, and returns it. This keeps the persistence/back-fill logic in the service layer.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The `addOwner` household branch now: if `sharesHousehold` is true, calls `joinHousehold` to link and stamp the shared id; otherwise keeps the existing 409 duplicate behavior. MapStruct maps `householdId` onto the response automatically.\n\nThe mapper needed no change (MapStruct maps `householdId` by name), and MapStruct's field mapping plus the shared normalizer keep the logic DRY. `mvnw test` reports `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` acceptance test is green.",
